- Affected when the player's action involves perception, investigation, searching,
  examining, recalling lore, detecting magic, tracking, hunting, foraging, or any
  Survival-based field activity. Passive observation ("I look around") IS affected
  — exploration domain is aware of the environment at all times.
- Exploration also owns stealth-style field actions: hiding, sneaking, moving quietly,
  shadowing someone, or trying to avoid notice. When the player is attempting stealth,
  this domain is responsible for that judgment.

- Passive observation, ambient awareness, and casual glancing still belong here when the player
  is simply perceiving the environment.
- Specific searching, trap-finding, tracking, hunting, foraging, recalling lore, and stealthy
  movement all belong here when the player is actively trying to learn or avoid being noticed.
- Using a detection spell or magic item to sense the environment is exploration, not inventory.
